<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Biograd na Moru</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Biograd na Moru is a coastal town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zadar</a>. It was one of the royal seats of the medieval Croatian kings and the seat of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>, and in 1102 Coloman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was crowned king of Croatia and Dalmatia there. Venetian forces destroyed it in 1125, and it later recovered as a small port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/biograd-na-moru.jpg" alt="Biograd na Moru" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: japus · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biograd-na-more-1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
